    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's what I implemented for the GOLD membership tier rule.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` was previously a pure function of a single owner's own fields (`namesakeCount`, `email`), derived at read-time by `OwnerMapper`. The new GOLD rule depends on the household's size \u2014 information not derivable from one owner's fields \u2014 so I followed the existing `namesakeCount` pattern: compute the household size once at creation and store it, keeping tier derivation deterministic from stored fields.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a stored `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with accessors, and extended `membershipTier(...)` to take `householdSize`: returns `'GOLD'` when it is \u2265 3, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 Added `countHouseholdMembers(owner)`, which counts existing owners sharing the same `householdId` (same normalized last name + address) plus the owner itself, and set it on create (right alongside `namesakeCount`), so the value reflects the household \"after this create\".\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `formatMembershipTier` now passes `owner.getHouseholdSize()` through.\n\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `household_size` column. hsqldb is what the tests use (`ddl-auto=none`, schema from SQL).\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` passes (third household member reads back `GOLD`), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nNote: the repo isn't a git repository, so I made no commit. Let me know if you'd like me to initialize one and commit.",
