        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing patterns of this codebase and a maintainer would find it natural.\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** The pure tier derivation stays on `Owner.membershipTier(...)` alongside its siblings (`membershipNumber`, `householdId`), extended with a third parameter rather than relocated. The data-dependent counting lives in `ClinicServiceImpl.countHouseholdMembers(...)` as a private helper, exactly where `countNamesakes` and `generateCustomerCode` live. Persisted field + getter/setter sit with the other owner fields.\n\n- **It mirrors the established idiom.** `countHouseholdMembers` uses the same `ownerRepository.findAll().stream().filter(exclude-self-by-id).filter(criterion).count()` shape as `countNamesakes`, `generateCustomerCode`, and `assertHouseholdIsUnique`. The guarded `if (owner.isNew() && owner.getHouseholdSize() == null)` stanza in `saveOwner` is a copy of the adjacent namesake stanza. Null-field short-circuit (`return 1`) matches `countNamesakes`'s `return 0`.\n\n- **No catch-all growth.** Each class gained only what belongs to it; nothing is duplicated into a new location. The slight overlap between `countHouseholdMembers` (matches on `householdId`) and `assertHouseholdIsUnique` (matches on `normalizeHousehold`/`normalizeAddress`) is the pre-existing house style \u2014 every derivation scans independently \u2014 so it's consistent rather than a new smell.\n\n- **Supporting surfaces are updated coherently and completely:** all four DB schemas, the OpenAPI description, the mapper delegation, and the three Javadocs (mapper, `membershipTier`, new helper) all reflect the new field."
